{"uid":"20d106364f238ee6","name":"test_in_flight_collision_within_single_sync","fullName":"tests.test_collision_fallback.TestCollisionFallback#test_in_flight_collision_within_single_sync","historyId":"b643a6d7e6e9336c586a3498e9ac2b76","time":{"start":1791160132195,"stop":1791160132197,"duration":2},"description":"The same-sync, both-new race: two distinct iCloud photos with\n        identical human filename, neither on disk yet. Without the in-flight\n        check, both ``collect_download_task`` calls return tasks pointing at\n        the SAME plain path; the later parallel download silently overwrites\n        the earlier one and we lose data (CWE-200-ish for a backup tool).\n\n        Models the scenario by passing the FIRST task's plain path as a\n        pre-populated entry in the shared ``files`` set (which is what the\n        real collection loop does between sequential calls), then asserting\n        the SECOND call sees the in-flight collision and routes to a suffix.\n        ","descriptionHtml":"<p>The same-sync, both-new race: two distinct iCloud photos with<br />\nidentical human filename, neither on disk yet. Without the in-flight<br />\ncheck, both <code>collect_download_task</code> calls return tasks pointing at<br />\nthe SAME plain path; the later parallel download silently overwrites<br />\nthe earlier one and we lose data (CWE-200-ish for a backup tool).</p>\n<pre><code>    Models the scenario by passing the FIRST task's plain path as a\n    pre-populated entry in the shared ``files`` set (which is what the\n    real collection loop does between sequential calls), then asserting\n    the SECOND call sees the in-flight collision and routes to a suffix.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"_unittest_setUpClass_fixture_TestCollisionFallback","time":{"start":1791160132181,"stop":1791160132181,"duration":0},"status":